==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Duche]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Duche]]s spawn after 40.33 seconds<sup>1,210f</sup>, delay 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Duche]]s spawn after 40.67 seconds<sup>1,220f</sup>, delay 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Dagshund]]s spawn after 42.67 seconds<sup>1,280f</sup>, delay 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Stall with [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Wall Cat]] and build your Wallet and Worker cat. At least 40 or so seconds into the battle, Dagshund appears quickly followed by several Duches. Then a second round of Dagshunds and Duches come out. When the second round is finished off, you should be able to knock out the base quickly.

You can also beat the level with a few meatshields and a stack of strong [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]].

Alternatively, you can use a Starting Money UP combo (Preferably [[Crazy Hearts (Combo)|Crazy Hearts]]) to spawn courier at the beginning and destroying the base before the Dagshunds and Duches come out.

